    "created_at": "2026-09-30T19:03:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-30T20:30:44Z",
    "body": "It would be better to return a failure flag (or a result like -1.0) in the instance where $L < D_\\text{MMC}+1$, as this is not a condition that could yield a reasonable test. Indeed, this testing requires that $L >= 1000000$ for SP 800-90B use. There surely is no point in continuing to use this estimator for such small datasets.\r\n\r\nThis is a real bug, but this correction shouldn't have any impact on past or future testing for data sets are are of a valid size.\r\n\r\nThis would be addressed by enforcing a 1000000 sample minimum.",
