    "updated_at": "2026-09-30T23:20:29Z",
    "body": "Thanks — agreed. The 1,000,000-sample minimum makes sense as the primary user-facing guard, and I agree that an invalid estimator length should return failure/no-result rather than continue.\n\nFor #268 specifically, would you prefer that I revise this PR to return failure locally as defense-in-depth, or supersede it with the central 1,000,000-sample intake check?\n",
