    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T04:33:36Z",
    "body": "My preference (which isn't really that relevant, but you asked) is to both make the in-estimator sanity checking occur using asserts (and leave assert checking in the final production binaries), and then force the central restriction programmatically, but I'm of the \"fail quickly and noisily\" religion. The NIST folks may have more relevant feedback on the issue. :-)",
